# Every path rule here is anchored with a leading slash so it matches only at
# the repo root. Unanchored, `.claude/commands/` would also match
# plugins/cairn/.claude/commands/ and silently untrack every plugin's shipped
# slash commands — the same trap that hid temper's own command file for months
# (a bare `TEMPER.md` pattern matched .claude/commands/temper.md at depth).

# Plan and review output.
#
# The suite's own tools write here: /critique-plan writes CRITIQUE.md,
# /critique-diff appends TEMPER.md, and enforce-whetstone.sh drops a
# .whetstone-nudged sentinel. It is per-developer, per-session scratch
# and means nothing in someone else's checkout — the convention itself is
# documented in templates/CLAUDE.md, which is versioned.
/.claude/plans/

# Artifacts of a local install.
#
# This repo is the installer, so `bash install.sh` without --global writes its
# output straight into the working tree: the suite hook and its gates, copies of
# every plugin's slash commands, the CLI, and the manifest. All are generated
# from files that are already versioned under plugins/.
#
# /.claude/settings.json is deliberately absent: a project may want to share it.
/.claude/hooks/
/.claude/commands/
/.claude/aether.manifest
/.bin/

# Backups written before install.sh and uninstall.sh mutate settings.json or
# CLAUDE.md in place.
*.bak

# macOS
.DS_Store
